        "nobel_worthiness": "Chaperonin-assisted folding changed the understanding of how proteins attain native structure in cells and supplied a fundamental framework for proteostasis.",
        "attribution": "Hartl and Horwich are closely and distinctly identified with the seminal demonstration of chaperonin-mediated folding.",
        "maturity": "The result is a mature cornerstone of molecular cell biology with sustained explanatory power.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Its very broad conceptual legacy makes the boundary with other chaperone discoveries relevant."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 8,
